From f642d89f4818638f070693c4522533118816f0f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Musichen <alex.musichen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:16:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(blends): the registry page shows what exists instead
 of seven invented previews

The /blends page listed seven "Preview - not published" Blends (ACRYL, Blank Canvas, Agent Workbench, Local-first Studio, Secure Ops, Data Pipeline, Release Pilot) with fictional plugin names, above the six starters that are really in the registry. A reader could not tell which half was real.

- The invented list is removed with its data: src/lib/content.ts no longer carries the preview array, BlendDetail only renders entries of registry/index.json, and the search panel, the category and subcategory pages and the vite route list read the registry instead.
- The page now says what a Blend is made of today: a framework map in spec 049's order (core, routing, serving, records, tiny data, live state, UI, desktop, agents, the door, live plugins, tooling), each row with the service a plugin injects, the real provider packages, and whether it is stable, optional or experimental. It is the same map as the spec, so the site and the spec can be compared line by line.
- src/lib/registry-placement.ts places each published starter in the 100-category taxonomy (the registry's own category field is the publisher's short word, not the taxonomy), so a category page shows the real entries that belong to it instead of always "No Blends here yet".
- The hero count is now "6 starters in the registry - 100 categories".

Verified with bun run build (722 real routes) and a headless pass over /blends, /blends/application and /blends/software-factories.
